From 20f219cb21c7f779a2ce0da37598666833de1df1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 12:59:58 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(ui): mark a warned path's moves in the viewport and
 frame them from the op page

Every move a verify warning names (gouge, shank/holder, rapid in
stock, fixture, crossing, envelope, sweep, scallop) now draws in the
colour-vision palette's gouge colour instead of its feed/rapid/plunge
colour, and the first move of each folded warning line carries a small
3-axis cross in that colour. Each folded warning line on the op page's
status banner is a link: a click centres the camera on that move
(view state, no command, zoom kept).

The move set is a pure app function (app::warned_moves) over the cached
warning list; indices past the path's end are dropped, never indexed.
RestUnjudged locates nothing and marks nothing. The per-path overlay
loop moves out of interact.rs into ui::path_lines; a path with no
warnings draws exactly what it drew before.

Refs #261

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
